<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19810" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βέομαι</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βείομαι</span></b> , Homeric subj. used as
		fut., I <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shall
			live</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔ τι Διὸς βέομαι φρεσίν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.194
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ αὐτὸς δηρὸν βέῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					16.852
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				24.131
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί νυ βείομαι αἰνὰ παθοῦσα</span>”
				<i>;</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					22.431
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιόμεσθα, βίονται</span> (v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιόω</span>), whence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίομαι, βίε᾽</span> should perh. be restored
			in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
